@* The lost-connection banners under the header (handoff D30): red when /healthz fails too (the map dims), amber when only
   the live link dropped (tiles still load over plain HTTP), red when the server stopped. They replace Blazor's reconnect
   dialog. The circuit is down while they show, so js/serve-live.js drives them: it marks <html data-link="…">, fills
   the countdown and handles Try now. Nothing here changes after the first render. *@
<div class="link-banner" data-link-banner="disconnected" role="alert">
    <Icon Name="wifi-off" Size="16" />
    <span class="link-banner-text"><span class="strong">Can't reach the server.</span> The map keeps what it has. <span data-link-countdown></span></span>
    <button type="button" class="button link-retry" data-link-retry><Icon Name="refresh" Size="15" /> Try now</button>
</div>
<div class="link-banner link-banner-warn" data-link-banner="reconnecting" role="status">
    <Icon Name="wifi-off" Size="16" />
    <span class="link-banner-text"><span class="strong">Live updates paused.</span> Reconnecting… Tiles still load.</span>
    <button type="button" class="button link-retry" data-link-retry><Icon Name="refresh" Size="15" /> Try now</button>
</div>
<div class="link-banner" data-link-banner="stopped" role="alert">
    <Icon Name="wifi-off" Size="16" />
    <span class="link-banner-text"><span class="strong">The server stopped.</span> The map keeps what it has. The page reloads when the server is back.</span>
    <button type="button" class="button link-retry" data-link-retry><Icon Name="refresh" Size="15" /> Try now</button>
</div>
